{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"context free grammar context free grammar","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md","fileName":"Context-Free Grammar.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Context-Free Grammar","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Natural Language Understanding Systems]] · [[Context-Free Languages and Parsing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Natural Language Understanding Systems","Context-Free Languages and Parsing","Meaning Representation","Production Rule","Derivation","aiassistants.epub","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"context free grammar context free grammar","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md","fileName":"Context-Free Grammar.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Context-Free Grammar","heading":"Context-Free Grammar","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A context-free grammar describes how symbols can be combined using production rules. Terminal symbols correspond to words or tokens, while nonterminal symbols represent categories such as phrases, slots, or requests.\n\nFor a narrow assistant domain, a grammar can both recognize valid utterances and construct a [[Meaning Representation]]. Coverage and maintenance become difficult as users introduce unanticipated wording.\n\nFormally, a context-free grammar is a four-tuple containing nonterminal symbols, terminal symbols, [[Production Rule|production rules]], and a start symbol. Starting from that symbol, a [[Derivation]] generates a language by repeatedly replacing a nonterminal without regard to its surrounding context.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Natural Language Understanding Systems","Context-Free Languages and Parsing","Meaning Representation","Production Rule","Derivation","aiassistants.epub","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"context free grammar context free grammar","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Context-Free Grammar.md","fileName":"Context-Free Grammar.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Context-Free Grammar","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Natural Language Understanding Systems","Context-Free Languages and Parsing","Meaning Representation","Production Rule","Derivation","aiassistants.epub","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}